{
  "_id": "6afcdd5fef1f2edb4068544b",
  "Package": "woven",
  "Title": "Weighted Omics View Embedding via Nystrom for Incomplete\nMulti-Omics Data",
  "Version": "0.99.6",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\"Nathan\", \"Bresette\",\nrole = c(\"aut\", \"cre\"),\nemail = \"nathanbresette04@gmail.com\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0009-0003-1554-6006\")),\nperson(\"Ai-Ling\", \"Lin\",\nrole = \"aut\"),\nperson(\"Jianlin\", \"Cheng\",\nrole = \"aut\"),\nperson(\"National Institutes of Health / National Institute on Aging\",\nrole = \"fnd\",\ncomment = \"R56AG079586\")\n)",
  "Description": "Supervised multi-omics integration for block-missing\n(\"ragged\") data, where some subjects lack one or more whole\nomics modalities (assay blocks) rather than scattered\nindividual values. WOVEN fits a shared latent space with SUMCOR\n(sum of correlations) multi-set canonical correlation analysis,\na criterion that maximizes the summed pairwise correlation\nbetween modalities' latent scores, using only the anchor\nsubjects observed in every modality; class labels enter through\na label-augmented cross-covariance, and per-modality graph\nLaplacians regularize the fit. Every other subject is then\nscored from the modalities it has by a Nystrom extension, a way\nto place new points in an already fitted embedding (for WOVEN's\nlinear embedding, multiplying the observed features by the\nlearned projection matrices), so no missing block is imputed.\nThe effective sample size (ESS) retention, the fraction of\nsubjects a method can score, is therefore the fraction with at\nleast one observed modality, rather than the complete-case\nfraction. woven_tune() chooses the regularization settings by\ncross-validated balanced error rate, and the fitted model is\nsummarized by plots and a table of the top features per\nmodality.",
